  "instruction": "Among Saia, Inc., Matson, Inc., and ArcBest Corporation, which company had the greatest reduction in operating expenses for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2023? Use the SEC website and filings.",
  "answer": "Based on the research from SEC 10-K filings, here are the findings:\n\n## Operating Expense Comparison FY2023 vs FY2022\n\n| Company | 2022 Operating Expenses | 2023 Operating Expenses | Change | % Change |\n|---------|------------------------|------------------------|--------|----------|\n| **Saia, Inc.** | $2,321.6M | $2,420.9M | **+$99.4M (increase)** | **+4.28% (increase)** |\n| **Matson, Inc.** | $2,989.4M | $2,751.8M | **-$237.6M (reduction)** | **-7.95%** |\n| **ArcBest Corporation** | $4,634.5M | $4,254.8M | **-$379.7M (reduction)** | **-8.19%** |\n\n## Answer\n\n**ArcBest Corporation** had the greatest reduction in operating expenses for the fiscal year ended December 31, 2023.\n\n- **Absolute reduction**: ArcBest reduced operating expenses by **$379.7 million**, compared to Matson's $237.6 million reduction. Saia actually *increased* operating expenses by $99.4 million.\n- **Percentage reduction**: ArcBest achieved an **8.19%** reduction, compared to Matson's 7.95%.\n\n## Sources\n\n1. **Saia, Inc.** — 10-K filed Feb 2024: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1177702/000095017024019368/saia-20231231.htm (Item 8, Consolidated Statements of Operations, \"Total operating expenses\")\n2. **Matson, Inc.** — 10-K filed Feb 23, 2024: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/3453/000155837024001570/matx-20231231x10k.htm (Item 8, Consolidated Statements of Income, \"Total Costs and Expenses\")\n3. **ArcBest Corporation** — 10-K filed Feb 23, 2024: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/894405/000155837024001622/arcb-20231231x10k.htm (Item 8, Consolidated Statements of Operations, \"Total operating expenses\")",
